ymentProvider.cs:62-66`)/(`src\\/DcaShop.Checkout\\/Application\\/Shared\\/IPaymentProvider.cs:69-73`)/' -e 's/(`IPaymentProvider.cs:45-50`)/(`IPaymentProvider.cs:50-52`)/' $f && grep -n 'cs:' $f","description":"Fix cited line numbers in judge.md"}}],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":29,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"The judge stage passed `pay-through-the-provider`, so the story can be delivered. The verdict is in `tasks/pay-through-the-provider/judge.md`. I changed no code and ran no tests; I only reviewed the recorded diff.\n\n**Previous round — all three defects are fixed:**\n- **Major (missing scenario):** the shared specification now has `scenario.checkout.provider-authorizes-payment` (`scenarios.md:35-42`). The browser test's display name matches its title (`ProviderPaymentE2eTest.cs:23`). The Java sample's `ProviderPaymentE2ETest` uses the same title, so the two suites stay in step.\n- **Minor (cancelling answered \"refused\"):** the port now documents that `Refused` also covers an operation the provider doesn't offer (`IPaymentProvider.cs:69-73`).\n- **Minor (public constructor):** `PaymentResult` now has a private constructor, so only its three factory methods can create one (`IPaymentProvider.cs:50-52`).\n\n**This round:** the DDD, hexagonal, clean-code and DCA reviews each ran through the skill the profile names for it. None found a new defect. All three acceptance criteria are met by behaviour, and nothing out of scope was delivered.\n\nFour small points were considered and recorded as not blocking:\n- The Checkout glossary still says the provider's own reason reaches the customer. The page now shows fixed texts, so this is left to the documentation stage, which runs next.\n- The browser test's method name no longer matches its new display name. The test stage kept it on purpose because the gate's criterion table uses the method name.\n- A reference check in `SubmitPaymentUseCase` is now redundant but harmless.\n- An unavailable payment is logged twice, once by the adapter and once by the use case. Each log line carries different detail.","ttft_ms":12249,"type":"result","duration_ms":124387,"uuid":"9da0ceb5-7755-487c-b612-6209cf7a1113","ttft_stream_ms":10949,"time_to_request_ms":75,"first_content_frame_ms":10949,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
